(function(E){ const x = E["exam-05"] = E["exam-05"] || {units:{}}; (x.units = x.units || {})["x05-l2"] = {"id":"x05-l2","patterns":["L2-tours"],"title":{"en":"Listening Part 2: a visit to a workshop","tr":"Listening Part 2: bir atölye ziyareti","fa":"Listening Part 2: بازدید از یک کارگاه"},"objective":{"en":"In this lesson you will learn to follow one speaker who welcomes visitors: choose the right answer when all three options are mentioned, and pick the two things that are true from a list of five.","tr":"Bu derste ziyaretçileri karşılayan tek bir konuşmacıyı takip etmeyi öğreneceksin: üç seçeneğin hepsinden söz edildiğinde doğru cevabı seçecek ve beş maddelik bir listeden doğru olan ikisini bulacaksın.","fa":"در این درس یاد می‌گیری حرف‌های یک نفر را که از بازدیدکننده‌ها استقبال می‌کند دنبال کنی: وقتی از هر سه گزینه حرف زده می‌شود جواب درست را انتخاب کنی و از یک فهرست پنج‌تایی دو موردِ درست را پیدا کنی."},"sessions":[["explain"],["drill"],["exit"]],"explain":{"title":{"en":"Listening Part 2: a visit to a workshop","tr":"Listening Part 2: bir atölye ziyareti","fa":"Listening Part 2: بازدید از یک کارگاه"},"objective":{"en":"In this lesson you will learn to follow one speaker who welcomes visitors: choose the right answer when all three options are mentioned, and pick the two things that are true from a list of five.","tr":"Bu derste ziyaretçileri karşılayan tek bir konuşmacıyı takip etmeyi öğreneceksin: üç seçeneğin hepsinden söz edildiğinde doğru cevabı seçecek ve beş maddelik bir listeden doğru olan ikisini bulacaksın.","fa":"در این درس یاد می‌گیری حرف‌های یک نفر را که از بازدیدکننده‌ها استقبال می‌کند دنبال کنی: وقتی از هر سه گزینه حرف زده می‌شود جواب درست را انتخاب کنی و از یک فهرست پنج‌تایی دو موردِ درست را پیدا کنی."},"stats":[{"label":{"en":"Questions","tr":"Soru","fa":"سؤال"},"value":"10"},{"label":{"en":"Speakers","tr":"Konuşan","fa":"گوینده"},"value":"1"},{"label":{"en":"Question types","tr":"Soru türü","fa":"نوع سؤال"},"value":{"en":"A-C, then choose TWO","tr":"A-C, sonra İKİ seç","fa":"A-C، بعد دو تا انتخاب کن"}}],"context":{"eyebrow":{"en":"1 The context","tr":"1 Bağlam","fa":"۱ بافت"},"head":{"en":"This exam: a glass-blowing studio","tr":"Bu sınav: bir cam üfleme atölyesi","fa":"این آزمون: یک کارگاه شیشه‌گری"},"intro":{"en":"Part 2 is one person talking to a group: a guide, an organiser or a local expert. Tours and visitor talks are the most common Part 2 situation. The talk moves from history to practical information, and the questions follow it.","tr":"Part 2, bir gruba konuşan tek bir kişidir: bir rehber, bir organizatör ya da yerel bir uzman. Turlar ve ziyaretçi konuşmaları Part 2’de en sık çıkan durumdur. Konuşma tarihten pratik bilgilere geçer ve sorular onu izler.","fa":"Part 2 یک نفر است که با یک گروه حرف می‌زند: یک راهنما، یک برگزارکننده یا یک کارشناس محلی. تورها و صحبت برای بازدیدکننده‌ها رایج‌ترین موقعیت Part 2 هستند. صحبت از تاریخچه به اطلاعات عملی می‌رسد و سؤال‌ها هم همین مسیر را می‌روند."},"technique":{"en":"2 The technique","tr":"2 Teknik","fa":"۲ تکنیک"},"labels":{"asks":{"en":"What this part is about","tr":"Bu kısım ne hakkında","fa":"این بخش درباره‌ی چیست"},"fields":{"en":"Headings you will see","tr":"Göreceğin başlıklar","fa":"عنوان‌هایی که می‌بینی"},"words":{"en":"Words that carry the answers","tr":"Cevabı taşıyan kelimeler","fa":"کلمه‌هایی که جواب را می‌آورند"},"a":{"en":"On the paper","tr":"Kâğıtta","fa":"روی برگه"},"b":{"en":"What you hear or read","tr":"Duyduğun ya da okuduğun","fa":"چیزی که می‌شنوی یا می‌خوانی"},"traps":{"en":"Traps","tr":"Tuzaklar","fa":"دام‌ها"},"example":{"en":"Example","tr":"Örnek","fa":"نمونه"},"ideas":{"en":"Ideas","tr":"Fikirler","fa":"ایده‌ها"}},"cards":[{"id":"x05-l2-ctx","exam":true,"patterns":["L2-tours"],"often":{"pattern":"L2-tours","n":13,"of":40,"label":{"en":"Comes up often in the real exam: 13 of the last 40 tests","tr":"Gerçek sınavda sık çıkar: son 40 sınavın 13’ünde","fa":"در آزمون واقعی زیاد می‌آید: در ۱۳ آزمون از ۴۰ آزمونِ اخیر"}},"title":{"en":"A talk at a craft workshop","tr":"Bir zanaat atölyesinde bir konuşma","fa":"صحبتی در یک کارگاه صنایع دستی"},"asks":{"en":"One speaker welcomes a group of visitors. First the history: why the craft began there, what the building used to be, who started the business and how it survives. Then the visit itself: the safety rules and what the group will do.","tr":"Bir konuşmacı bir ziyaretçi grubunu karşılıyor. Önce tarih: zanaatın orada neden başladığı, binanın eskiden ne olduğu, işi kimin kurduğu ve nasıl ayakta kaldığı. Sonra ziyaretin kendisi: güvenlik kuralları ve grubun ne yapacağı.","fa":"یک نفر از گروهی از بازدیدکننده‌ها استقبال می‌کند. اول تاریخچه: چرا این کار آن‌جا شروع شد، ساختمان قبلاً چه بود، چه کسی کار را راه انداخت و چطور سر پا مانده. بعد خودِ بازدید: قانون‌های ایمنی و کاری که گروه انجام می‌دهد."},"fields":["Why it started here","The building before","The founder’s aim","Where the money comes from","A recent change","What the speaker enjoys","Safety rules","What visitors will do"],"words":[{"a":"set up","b":"founded / started","tr":"kurmak","fa":"راه انداختن"},{"a":"main aim","b":"what she wanted most / the point was","tr":"asıl amaç","fa":"هدف اصلی"},{"a":"income","b":"what pays the bills / where the money comes from","tr":"gelir","fa":"درآمد"},{"a":"course","b":"class / taster day / workshop","tr":"kurs","fa":"دوره، کلاس"},{"a":"replaced","b":"changed it for a new one","tr":"yerine yenisini koydu","fa":"جایگزین کرد"},{"a":"apprentice","b":"a young person learning a craft from an expert","tr":"çırak","fa":"شاگرد، کارآموز"},{"a":"must","b":"I do insist on / you have to","tr":"zorunlu","fa":"حتماً باید"},{"a":"not allowed","b":"we stopped that / you won’t be able to","tr":"izin yok","fa":"ممنوع، مجاز نیست"},{"a":"demonstration","b":"someone shows you how they make it","tr":"gösteri, uygulama","fa":"نمایش عملی"},{"a":"transport","b":"boats could carry / bring in","tr":"taşıma","fa":"حمل‌ونقل"},{"a":"enjoy most","b":"what I love is","tr":"en çok sevdiği","fa":"بیشتر از همه دوست دارد"},{"a":"take home","b":"leave with it today","tr":"eve götürmek","fa":"با خودت به خانه بردن"}],"traps":[{"en":"Every option is mentioned, often in order. \"People assume it was the beach sand, but...\" The answer comes after but, actually or what really.","tr":"Her seçenekten söz edilir, çoğu zaman sırayla. \"İnsanlar sahildeki kum sanıyor ama...\" Cevap but, actually ya da what really’den sonra gelir.","fa":"از همه‌ی گزینه‌ها حرف زده می‌شود، اغلب به ترتیب. «مردم خیال می‌کنند ماسه‌ی ساحل بود، اما...». جواب بعد از but، actually یا what really می‌آید."},{"en":"\"Choose TWO\" rules: a rule from the past (\"we used to...\") or something \"you’re welcome to do\" is not a rule you must follow now.","tr":"\"İKİ seç\" kuralları: geçmişteki bir kural (\"eskiden ... yapardık\") ya da \"yapmakta serbestsin\" denen şey, şimdi uyman gereken bir kural değildir.","fa":"قانون‌های «دو تا انتخاب کن»: قانونی که مال گذشته است («قبلاً ... می‌کردیم») یا کاری که «آزادی انجامش بدهی» قانونی نیست که الان باید رعایتش کنی."},{"en":"A plan that is mentioned but stopped: \"We talked about a bigger café, but there isn’t room.\" Talked about is not done.","tr":"Söz edilen ama durdurulan bir plan: \"Daha büyük bir kafe konuştuk ama yer yok.\" Konuşulmuş olması yapılmış olması demek değil.","fa":"برنامه‌ای که گفته می‌شود ولی متوقف شده: «درباره‌ی یک کافه‌ی بزرگ‌تر حرف زدیم، ولی جا نیست». حرفش را زدن یعنی انجام نشده."}],"example":{"lines":[["Guide","Most people think the mill closed because of the floods. In fact, the river was fine; the owners simply couldn’t compete with the new factories in the north."]],"item":"Why did the mill close? A floods  B competition  C a fire","answer":"B","why":{"en":"Floods are what \"most people think\". \"In fact... couldn’t compete\" = competition.","tr":"Sel \"çoğu insanın sandığı\" şey. \"Aslında... rekabet edemedi\" = rekabet.","fa":"سیل چیزی است که «بیشتر مردم فکر می‌کنند». «در واقع... نتوانستند رقابت کنند» یعنی رقابت."}}},{"id":"L2-tours","ctx":["L2-tours"],"title":{"en":"Tours and visitor information","tr":"Turlar ve ziyaretçi bilgileri","fa":"تورها و اطلاعات بازدیدکننده"},"asks":{"en":"A guide or presenter tells visitors about a place: a heritage walk, a castle, a museum, a stadium, a boat trip. Questions ask about its history, what is new, what visitors can do, the rules and what the guide recommends.","tr":"Bir rehber ya da sunucu ziyaretçilere bir yeri anlatır: tarihî bir yürüyüş, bir kale, bir müze, bir stadyum, bir tekne gezisi. Sorular yerin tarihini, yeniliklerini, ziyaretçilerin neler yapabileceğini, kuralları ve rehberin tavsiyesini sorar.","fa":"یک راهنما یا مجری جایی را برای بازدیدکننده‌ها معرفی می‌کند: یک پیاده‌روی تاریخی، یک قلعه، یک موزه، یک ورزشگاه، یک گردش با قایق. سؤال‌ها درباره‌ی تاریخچه، چیزهای تازه، کارهایی که بازدیدکننده می‌تواند بکند، قانون‌ها و توصیه‌ی راهنماست."},"fields":["What was the building originally used for?","What has changed recently?","What does the guide recommend?","Which TWO activities are available today?","What are visitors not allowed to do?","What can visitors see in each area?"],"words":[{"a":"originally built as","b":"it started life as","tr":"aslen ... olarak yapılmış","fa":"در اصل به‌عنوان ... ساخته شده"},{"a":"restored","b":"brought back to how it looked","tr":"restore edilmiş","fa":"مرمت‌شده"},{"a":"exhibition","b":"the display / what's on show","tr":"sergi","fa":"نمایشگاه"},{"a":"not allowed","b":"please don't / you can't","tr":"yasak","fa":"ممنوع"},{"a":"recommend","b":"if you only have time for one thing","tr":"tavsiye etmek","fa":"توصیه کردن"},{"a":"recently opened","b":"it's only been open since","tr":"yeni açılmış","fa":"تازه باز شده"},{"a":"guided","b":"someone will take you round","tr":"rehberli","fa":"با راهنما"},{"a":"free","b":"it won't cost you anything","tr":"ücretsiz","fa":"رایگان"},{"a":"closed for repairs","b":"work is being done on","tr":"onarım için kapalı","fa":"به‌خاطر تعمیر بسته"},{"a":"souvenirs","b":"things to take home","tr":"hediyelik eşya","fa":"سوغاتی"},{"a":"most popular","b":"what people enjoy most","tr":"en popüler","fa":"پرطرفدارترین"},{"a":"the view","b":"you can see right across","tr":"manzara","fa":"منظره"}],"traps":[{"en":"Past and present: \"this was once the stables; today it’s the cafe\". The question usually asks about now.","tr":"Geçmiş ve şimdi: \"burası eskiden ahırdı; bugün kafe\". Soru genelde şimdiyi sorar.","fa":"گذشته و حال: «اینجا قبلاً اصطبل بود؛ امروز کافه است». سؤال معمولاً درباره‌ی حالاست."},{"en":"Every option is mentioned; one is \"temporarily closed\" or \"coming next year\".","tr":"Her seçenek söylenir; biri \"geçici olarak kapalı\" ya da \"gelecek yıl geliyor\" olur.","fa":"همه‌ی گزینه‌ها گفته می‌شوند؛ یکی «موقتاً بسته» است یا «سال آینده می‌آید»."},{"en":"Choose TWO: three activities are named, but one is only for groups or children.","tr":"İki seçenek seç: üç etkinlik sayılır ama biri yalnızca gruplar ya da çocuklar içindir.","fa":"انتخاب دو گزینه: سه فعالیت گفته می‌شود، ولی یکی فقط برای گروه‌ها یا بچه‌هاست."}],"example":{"lines":[["Guide","Many visitors head straight for the tower, and the view from the top is lovely."],["Guide","But if you only have time for one thing, I’d say go to the kitchens."],["Guide","They’re the oldest part of the castle and still have the original ovens."]],"item":"What does the guide recommend?  A the tower   B the kitchens   C the gardens","answer":"B","why":{"en":"The tower is popular, but \"if you only have time for one thing, I’d say\" introduces the recommendation: the kitchens.","tr":"Kule popüler ama \"if you only have time for one thing, I’d say\" tavsiyeyi getiriyor: mutfaklar.","fa":"برج پرطرفدار است، ولی «if you only have time for one thing, I’d say» توصیه را معرفی می‌کند: آشپزخانه‌ها."}},"general":true,"patterns":["L2-tours"],"often":{"pattern":"L2-tours","n":13,"of":40,"label":{"en":"Comes up often in the real exam: 13 of the last 40 tests","tr":"Gerçek sınavda sık çıkar: son 40 sınavın 13’ünde","fa":"در آزمون واقعی زیاد می‌آید: در ۱۳ آزمون از ۴۰ آزمونِ اخیر"}}}]},"points":[{"eyebrow":{"en":"In the exam","tr":"Sınavda","fa":"در آزمون"},"head":{"en":"Six A-C questions, then two pairs","tr":"Altı A-C sorusu, sonra iki çift","fa":"شش سؤال A-C، بعد دو جفت"},"body":{"en":"Questions 11-16: choose A, B or C. Questions 17-18 and 19-20: choose TWO letters from A-E; each correct letter is one mark, in any order. You read Questions 11-16 first and Questions 17-20 in the break.","tr":"Soru 11-16: A, B ya da C’yi seç. Soru 17-18 ve 19-20: A-E’den İKİ harf seç; her doğru harf bir puandır, sırası önemli değil. Önce Soru 11-16’yı, aradaki molada da Soru 17-20’yi okursun.","fa":"سؤال‌های ۱۱ تا ۱۶: A، B یا C را انتخاب کن. سؤال‌های ۱۷-۱۸ و ۱۹-۲۰: از A تا E دو حرف انتخاب کن؛ هر حرف درست یک نمره است و ترتیبش مهم نیست. اول سؤال‌های ۱۱ تا ۱۶ را می‌خوانی و در وقفه سؤال‌های ۱۷ تا ۲۰ را."}},{"eyebrow":{"en":"The method","tr":"Yöntem","fa":"روش"},"head":{"en":"Listen to the end of each point","tr":"Her noktanın sonuna kadar dinle","fa":"هر نکته را تا آخر گوش بده"},"steps":[{"en":"Underline the key word of each question: why, before, aim, income, change, enjoy.","tr":"Her sorunun anahtar kelimesinin altını çiz: why, before, aim, income, change, enjoy.","fa":"زیر کلمه‌ی کلیدی هر سؤال خط بکش: why، before، aim، income، change، enjoy."},{"en":"When you hear an option, do not choose it yet: the speaker may rule it out.","tr":"Bir seçeneği duyunca hemen seçme: konuşmacı onu eleyebilir.","fa":"وقتی یک گزینه را می‌شنوی، هنوز انتخابش نکن: ممکن است گوینده ردش کند."},{"en":"For choose TWO, mark each option yes or no as you hear it: must, not allowed, used to, instead.","tr":"İKİ seç sorularında her seçeneği duyduğun anda evet ya da hayır diye işaretle: must, not allowed, used to, instead.","fa":"در سؤال‌های «دو تا انتخاب کن»، هر گزینه را همان موقع که می‌شنوی با بله یا نه علامت بزن: must، not allowed، used to، instead."}]},{"eyebrow":{"en":"The trap","tr":"Tuzak","fa":"دام"},"head":{"en":"Mentioned is not the same as chosen","tr":"Söz edilmek seçilmek demek değil","fa":"گفته شدن یعنی انتخاب شدن نیست"},"body":{"en":"Wrong options are not invented: they are in the talk, but the speaker says they are not true, not now, or not the main thing. Listen for what other people assume, what used to happen and what was only discussed.","tr":"Yanlış seçenekler uydurma değildir: konuşmada geçerler ama konuşmacı onların doğru olmadığını, artık geçerli olmadığını ya da asıl şey olmadığını söyler. Başkalarının ne sandığına, eskiden ne olduğuna ve neyin yalnızca konuşulduğuna kulak ver.","fa":"گزینه‌های غلط ساختگی نیستند: در صحبت می‌آیند، اما گوینده می‌گوید درست نیستند، الان نیستند یا موضوع اصلی نیستند. به چیزی که دیگران خیال می‌کنند، چیزی که قبلاً اتفاق می‌افتاد و چیزی که فقط درباره‌اش حرف زده شده گوش بده."}}],"example":{"eyebrow":{"en":"Worked example","tr":"Çözümlü örnek","fa":"مثال حل‌شده"},"head":{"en":"Choose TWO, step by step","tr":"İKİ seç, adım adım","fa":"دو تا انتخاب کن، قدم به قدم"},"instruction":"Choose TWO letters, A-E. Which TWO things must visitors to the bakery do?","item":"A wash their hands  B wear a hat  C pay for the bread  D book a place  E bring an apron","lines":[["Guide","You don’t need to bring an apron, we have plenty. The bread is free, and there’s no need to book. But everyone must wash their hands at the sink by the door, and please put on one of the paper hats."]],"answer":"A and B","walk":[{"en":"Apron: \"you don’t need to bring\" = no.","tr":"Önlük: \"getirmen gerekmez\" = hayır.","fa":"پیش‌بند: «لازم نیست بیاوری» یعنی نه."},{"en":"Pay and book: \"free\" and \"no need to book\" = no.","tr":"Ödeme ve rezervasyon: \"ücretsiz\" ve \"rezervasyona gerek yok\" = hayır.","fa":"پرداخت و رزرو: «رایگان» و «نیازی به رزرو نیست» یعنی نه."},{"en":"\"Everyone must wash their hands\" and \"please put on one of the paper hats\" = A and B.","tr":"\"Herkes ellerini yıkamalı\" ve \"lütfen kâğıt şapkalardan birini takın\" = A ve B.","fa":"«همه باید دست‌هایشان را بشویند» و «لطفاً یکی از کلاه‌های کاغذی را سرتان بگذارید» یعنی A و B."}]},"quick":{"prompt":"\"Lots of visitors think we close in winter because of the cold, but actually it’s because the paths flood.\" Why does the place close in winter?","options":["the cold weather","fewer visitors","the paths flood"],"correct":2,"why":{"en":"The cold is what visitors think. \"But actually\" gives the real reason: the paths flood.","tr":"Soğuk, ziyaretçilerin sandığı şey. \"But actually\" asıl nedeni veriyor: yolları su basıyor.","fa":"سرما چیزی است که بازدیدکننده‌ها خیال می‌کنند. «but actually» دلیل واقعی را می‌دهد: مسیرها را آب می‌گیرد."}},"remember":{"en":"All the options are in the talk: wait for but, actually or what really, and check whether a rule is for now or for the past.","tr":"Seçeneklerin hepsi konuşmada geçer: but, actually ya da what really’yi bekle ve bir kuralın şimdi için mi geçmiş için mi olduğuna bak.","fa":"همه‌ی گزینه‌ها در صحبت هستند: منتظر but، actually یا what really بمان و ببین یک قانون مال الان است یا گذشته."},"type":"explain","id":"c-x05-l2-e","course":"ielts-exams","exam":"exam-05","unit":"x05-l2"},"drill":{"type":"drill","skill":"listening","part":"Listening Part 2","title":{"en":"Wren Lane Glass Studio","tr":"Wren Lane Cam Atölyesi","fa":"کارگاه شیشه‌ی رن لین"},"timed":7,"ctx":["L2-tours"],"script":[{"who":"Guide","line":"Good morning, everyone, and welcome to Wren Lane Glass Studio. My name's Daniel Shaw, and I've been blowing glass here for about twenty years. In a few minutes I'll take you into the workshop, but first I'd like to tell you a little about the building and how the studio started."},{"who":"Guide","line":"Glass has been made in this part of the town for two hundred years. People often assume it was because of the sand on the beach, but the local sand actually contains too much iron to make clear glass, and the coal for the furnaces had to come from forty miles away. What brought the glassmakers here in the 1820s was the canal. Boats could bring in materials cheaply and carry the finished bottles to the cities without breaking them on bumpy roads."},{"who":"Guide","line":"This building wasn't part of the original glassworks. When the last factory closed in 1961, it stood empty for a while, and then for nearly thirty years it was a garage for the town's buses. If you look at the floor in the shop, you can still see where the mechanics' pit used to be. Some visitors think it must have been a school, because of the bell on the roof, but that bell actually came from a church that was knocked down nearby."},{"who":"Guide","line":"The studio was set up in 1994 by my own teacher, Ruth Kessler. She sold a few pieces to tourists, of course, but making money was never the point for her. By then almost nobody in the country was passing on the old skills, and what she wanted most was a place where young people could learn the craft properly. Most of the glassmakers working here today started as her apprentices."},{"who":"Guide","line":"So how does a small studio like ours survive? We have the shop, which you'll see later, and now and then we make large pieces for hotels and restaurants. But neither of those pays the bills. These days most of our income comes from the courses we run for the public, from one-day tasters to ten-week evening classes."},{"who":"Guide","line":"The biggest change in the last few years has been the furnace. For decades we ran a gas furnace twenty-four hours a day, because it takes so long to heat up again. Two years ago we replaced it with an electric one. It cost a lot to install, but it's far cleaner and much quieter. We also talked about making the shop bigger, but there simply isn't room."},{"who":"Guide","line":"People sometimes ask me what I enjoy most about the job. It isn't the finished pieces, really. When I look at something I've made, I mostly see what went wrong. And I can promise you that the heat is no fun in August. Teaching is rewarding, but it's tiring too. What I love is the moment when the glass starts to move on the end of the pipe, and you've got about three seconds to decide what it's going to become."},{"who":"Guide","line":"Right, before we go through, a few words about safety in the workshop. You're welcome to take as many photographs as you like, and your bags are fine as long as you keep them under the benches. We used to give everyone safety glasses, but the glass screens in front of the benches protect you now, so you won't need them. There are two things I do insist on, though. First, please stay behind the yellow line painted on the floor at all times. The pipes swing round quickly and the glass is over a thousand degrees. And second, if you have long hair, please tie it back before you go in. I've got some spare hair bands here if anyone needs one."},{"who":"Guide","line":"Now, what's going to happen in there. I'm afraid you won't be blowing glass yourselves today. That needs proper training and a full class. We used to let visitors make a simple glass bead, but our insurance company stopped that last year. What each of you will do is choose two colours for a paperweight, and I'll make it in front of you, so you can see every stage."},{"who":"Guide","line":"Paperweights have to cool very slowly, overnight, or they crack, so you won't be able to take yours home today. We'll wrap it carefully and post it to you later in the week. And to finish, my colleague Anya will show you how she makes a tall vase, which is much harder than it looks. She's been doing it for eight years, and she still says she learns something every time."},{"who":"Guide","line":"So, if you'd all like to follow me through this door, mind the step, and we'll begin."}],"groups":[{"instruction":"Questions 11-16. Choose the correct letter, A, B or C.","qtype":"mcq","questions":[{"n":11,"kind":"mcq","prompt":"Why did glassmaking begin in this area?","options":["A The local sand was suitable.","B There was a canal for transport.","C Coal was cheap nearby."],"correct":1,"evidence":"What brought the glassmakers here in the 1820s was the canal","why":{"en":"The sand had \"too much iron\" and the coal came \"from forty miles away\". \"What brought the glassmakers here... was the canal.\"","tr":"Kumda \"çok fazla demir\" vardı, kömür de \"kırk mil öteden\" geliyordu. \"Cam ustalarını buraya getiren... kanaldı.\"","fa":"ماسه «آهن زیادی» داشت و زغال «از چهل مایل آن‌طرف‌تر» می‌آمد. «چیزی که شیشه‌گرها را به این‌جا آورد... کانال بود»."},"trap":["TR-ruledout","TR-paraphrase"]},{"n":12,"kind":"mcq","prompt":"What was the building used for before it became a studio?","options":["A a school","B a church","C a bus garage"],"correct":2,"evidence":"it was a garage for the town's buses","why":{"en":"The bell makes people think of a school, and it came from a church. For thirty years \"it was a garage for the town’s buses\".","tr":"Çan insanlara okulu düşündürüyor, kendisi de bir kiliseden geldi. Otuz yıl boyunca \"kasabanın otobüsleri için bir garajdı\".","fa":"زنگ آدم را یاد مدرسه می‌اندازد و از یک کلیسا آمده. سی سال «گاراژ اتوبوس‌های شهر بود»."},"trap":["TR-ruledout"]},{"n":13,"kind":"mcq","prompt":"What was Ruth Kessler’s main aim when she set up the studio?","options":["A to train young glassmakers","B to sell to tourists","C to make a profit"],"correct":0,"evidence":"a place where young people could learn the craft properly","why":{"en":"Tourists and money were \"never the point\". She wanted \"a place where young people could learn the craft properly\".","tr":"Turistler ve para \"hiçbir zaman amaç değildi\". \"Gençlerin zanaatı düzgünce öğrenebileceği bir yer\" istiyordu.","fa":"گردشگرها و پول «هیچ‌وقت هدف نبودند». او «جایی می‌خواست که جوان‌ها کار را درست یاد بگیرند»."},"trap":["TR-ruledout","TR-paraphrase"]},{"n":14,"kind":"mcq","prompt":"Where does most of the studio’s income come from today?","options":["A its shop","B work for hotels","C courses for the public"],"correct":2,"evidence":"most of our income comes from the courses we run for the public","why":{"en":"\"Neither of those pays the bills\": the shop and the hotel work are ruled out. Most income comes from courses.","tr":"\"Hiçbiri faturaları ödemiyor\": dükkân ve otel işleri eleniyor. Gelirin çoğu kurslardan geliyor.","fa":"«هیچ‌کدامشان خرج را درنمی‌آورد»: مغازه و کار برای هتل‌ها رد می‌شوند. بیشتر درآمد از دوره‌ها می‌آید."},"trap":["TR-ruledout"]},{"n":15,"kind":"mcq","prompt":"What change has the studio made recently?","options":["A It has enlarged its shop.","B It has installed a new furnace.","C It has opened for longer hours."],"correct":1,"evidence":"we replaced it with an electric one","why":{"en":"A bigger shop was only discussed (\"there simply isn’t room\"). Two years ago the gas furnace was replaced with an electric one.","tr":"Daha büyük dükkân yalnızca konuşuldu (\"yer yok\"). İki yıl önce gazlı fırın elektrikliyle değiştirildi.","fa":"مغازه‌ی بزرگ‌تر فقط در حد حرف بود («جا نیست»). دو سال پیش کوره‌ی گازی با یک کوره‌ی برقی عوض شد."},"trap":["TR-ruledout"]},{"n":16,"kind":"mcq","prompt":"What does Daniel enjoy most about his work?","options":["A the point at which the hot glass first alters its form","B looking at the finished pieces","C teaching beginners"],"correct":0,"evidence":"the moment when the glass starts to move on the end of the pipe","why":{"en":"He mostly sees \"what went wrong\" in finished pieces, and teaching is \"tiring too\". He loves \"the moment when the glass starts to move\".","tr":"Bitmiş parçalarda çoğunlukla \"neyin yanlış gittiğini\" görüyor, öğretmek de \"yorucu\". Sevdiği şey \"camın hareket etmeye başladığı an\".","fa":"در کار تمام‌شده بیشتر «اشکال‌ها» را می‌بیند و درس دادن هم «خسته‌کننده است». چیزی که دوست دارد «لحظه‌ای است که شیشه شروع به حرکت می‌کند»."},"trap":["TR-ruledout","TR-paraphrase"]}]},{"instruction":"Questions 17-18. Choose TWO letters, A-E.","qtype":"mcq2","questions":[{"n":17,"n2":18,"kind":"mcq2","prompt":"Which TWO rules must visitors follow in the workshop?","options":["A wear safety glasses","B leave their bags outside","C stay behind a line on the floor","D put away their cameras","E tie back long hair"],"correct":[2,4],"evidence":"please stay behind the yellow line painted on the floor","trap":["TR-ruledout"],"why":{"en":"Photos and bags are allowed, and safety glasses \"used to\" be given out. \"I do insist on\": the yellow line (C) and tying back long hair (E).","tr":"Fotoğraf ve çantalara izin var, gözlükler ise \"eskiden\" veriliyordu. \"Kesinlikle istediğim\": sarı çizgi (C) ve uzun saçı toplamak (E).","fa":"عکس و کیف مجازند و عینک ایمنی را «قبلاً» می‌دادند. «رویش اصرار دارم»: خط زرد (C) و بستن موی بلند (E)."}}]},{"instruction":"Questions 19-20. Choose TWO letters, A-E.","qtype":"mcq2","questions":[{"n":19,"n2":20,"kind":"mcq2","prompt":"Which TWO things will the visitors do in the workshop today?","options":["A make a glass bead","B decide on the colours of a paperweight","C blow a small bowl","D take a paperweight home","E watch someone make a vase"],"correct":[1,4],"evidence":"choose two colours for a paperweight","trap":["TR-ruledout","TR-paraphrase"],"why":{"en":"No blowing today, beads were stopped by the insurance company, and the paperweight is posted later. They choose colours (B) and watch Anya make a vase (E).","tr":"Bugün üfleme yok, boncuğu sigorta şirketi durdurdu, ağırlık da sonra postalanacak. Renk seçecekler (B) ve Anya’nın vazo yapışını izleyecekler (E).","fa":"امروز دمیدنی در کار نیست، مهره‌سازی را شرکت بیمه متوقف کرده و وزنه‌ی کاغذ بعداً پست می‌شود. رنگ انتخاب می‌کنند (B) و ساختن گلدان را از آنیا تماشا می‌کنند (E)."}}]}],"audio":{"voices":{"Announcer":{"accent":"British (standard Southern)","gender":"M","tts":{"engine":"kokoro","voice":"bm_george"},"role":"Recorded rubric"},"Guide":{"accent":"North American","gender":"M","tts":{"engine":"kokoro","voice":"am_michael"},"role":"Glass-blower who runs the studio"}},"sequence":[{"type":"announcer","text":"Part 2. You will hear a glass-blower talking to a group of visitors at his studio. First, you have some time to look at Questions 11 to 16."},{"type":"pause","seconds":30,"note":"reading time, Questions 11-16"},{"type":"announcer","text":"Now listen carefully and answer Questions 11 to 16."},{"type":"sfx","note":"large room with a faint low roar of a furnace in the background"},{"type":"lines","from":0,"to":6},{"type":"announcer","text":"Before you hear the rest of the talk, you have some time to look at Questions 17 to 20."},{"type":"pause","seconds":30,"note":"reading time, Questions 17-20"},{"type":"announcer","text":"Now listen and answer Questions 17 to 20."},{"type":"lines","from":7,"to":10},{"type":"announcer","text":"That is the end of Part 2. You now have half a minute to check your answers.","after":30}]},"id":"c-x05-l2-d","course":"ielts-exams","exam":"exam-05","unit":"x05-l2"},"exit":{"type":"exit","items":[{"tests":"paraphrase","point":3,"prompt":"An option says \"the main aim\". Which words in a talk mean the same?","options":["she sometimes thought about","what she wanted most was","one thing she tried was"],"correct":1,"why":{"en":"\"What she wanted most\" = her main aim.","tr":"\"En çok istediği şey\" = asıl amacı.","fa":"«چیزی که بیشتر از همه می‌خواست» یعنی هدف اصلی‌اش."}},{"tests":"word","point":1,"prompt":"\"Most of the bakers here started as her apprentices.\" An apprentice is...","options":["a young person learning a skill from an expert","a customer who buys a lot","a teacher at a college"],"correct":0,"why":{"en":"An apprentice learns a craft by working with someone skilled.","tr":"Çırak, usta biriyle çalışarak bir zanaatı öğrenir.","fa":"کارآموز با کار کنار یک استادکار، فن را یاد می‌گیرد."}},{"tests":"method","point":2,"prompt":"Choose TWO from A-E. You hear option D: \"You’re welcome to bring your dog.\" The question asks what visitors must do. What do you do with D?","options":["Mark it yes: it is mentioned","Wait for the end of the talk to decide","Mark it no: it is allowed, not required"],"correct":2,"why":{"en":"\"You’re welcome to\" means it is allowed, not a rule you must follow.","tr":"\"Yapmakta serbestsin\" izin demektir, uyman gereken bir kural değil.","fa":"«آزادی که...» یعنی مجاز است، نه قانونی که باید رعایتش کنی."}},{"tests":"trap","point":3,"prompt":"\"We thought about opening a café, but the council said no.\" Which statement is true?","options":["There is a new café.","There is no café.","A café will open next year."],"correct":1,"why":{"en":"A plan that was \"thought about\" and then refused did not happen.","tr":"\"Düşünülen\" ve sonra reddedilen bir plan gerçekleşmedi.","fa":"برنامه‌ای که «به آن فکر شد» و بعد رد شد، اجرا نشده."}},{"tests":"trap","point":2,"prompt":"\"Visitors used to make candles, but now they decorate one instead.\" What will visitors do today?","options":["decorate a candle","make a candle","watch candles being made"],"correct":0,"why":{"en":"\"Used to\" = the past; \"now... instead\" = what happens today.","tr":"\"Used to\" = geçmiş; \"now... instead\" = bugün olan.","fa":"«used to» یعنی گذشته؛ «now... instead» یعنی کاری که امروز انجام می‌شود."}}],"id":"c-x05-l2-x","course":"ielts-exams","exam":"exam-05","unit":"x05-l2"}}; })(globalThis.IELTS_EXAMS = globalThis.IELTS_EXAMS || {});
